# Keep out of Cursor's index. Two reasons: cost and correctness.
#
# Cost — indexing generated trees and vendored code burns embedding budget on files nobody
# will ever ask about.
# Correctness — an agent that retrieves a staged package, a build artifact or a backup will
# happily present stale content as current. Excluding them is a quality control, not tidiness.

# ── dependencies & build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/
.turbo/
.next/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# ── secrets: never index, never retrieve ──────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
secrets.json
load-secrets.ps1

# ── staged / generated QA packages ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated per ticket and superseded constantly. Indexing them means an agent can
# quote last sprint's spec as though it were the current one.
packages/staged_*/
allure-results/
allure-report/
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# ── backups & local state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.tmp
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── the eval harness's own fixtures ───────────────────────────────────────────
# eslint-plugin-qa-constitution/smoke/ holds a deliberately non-compliant spec, and
# lint-gate-eval/ holds generated files kept as evidence. Both are correct as artifacts
# and wrong as examples — an agent must not learn locator or assertion style from them.
eslint-plugin-qa-constitution/smoke/
eslint-plugin-qa-constitution/lint-gate-eval/

# ── large binaries ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.zip
*.7z
*.mp4
*.webm
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.pdf
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.pptx
